    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0141" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1950v02/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/9–2650: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-09-26T13:29:00-05:00">September 26,
                            1950—1:29 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Delga 36. Jebb told Gross September 25 p. m.,
                    Vishinsky had failed to respond to Jebb’s request for interview to discuss
                    appointment <pb facs="0142" n="126" xml:id="pg126"/> of SYG. With annoyance, Jebb said he thought the only course now
                    remaining was to put matter directly in GA. Gross
                    replied this course seemed premature at the moment and he would like to discuss
                    matter with Jebb again in next few days.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
